From: Korri downstream <maintainers@korri.invalid>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rendervulkan: make shader pipeline precompile optional

gamescope precompiles its entire compositing shader-permutation set
(BLIT/BLUR/BLUR_COND/RCAS/EASU/NIS/RGB_TO_NV12 across every layer count,
ycbcr mask, and blur-layer count) in a detached background thread at
device init. On fast conformant drivers (RADV/Adreno) this is a couple
of seconds. On PanVK's Bifrost-v7 compiler (Mali-G52 / Rockchip RK3566)
each pipeline compile takes seconds (full NIR optimisation + Bifrost
register allocation), so precompiling hundreds of permutations saturates
the single slow compiler for many minutes.

Worse, the per-frame on-demand pipeline() path compiles the pipeline it
needs while holding m_pipelineMutex; with the precompile thread hammering
the compiler, the first composite's pipeline is starved and the nested
present loop appears frozen on a single frame.

Add a GAMESCOPE_DISABLE_PIPELINE_PRECOMPILE env switch that skips the
precompile-everything thread. The on-demand pipeline() path still
compiles exactly the pipelines a given frame needs (one BLIT variant for
a simple fullscreen game) and the results are persisted to the Mesa
on-disk shader cache, so subsequent launches are fast too. On Adreno
(SM8550) and Steam-Deck-class hardware the env is unset and behaviour is
unchanged.
---
 src/rendervulkan.cpp | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/src/rendervulkan.cpp
+++ b/src/rendervulkan.cpp
@@ -317,8 +317,18 @@
 
 	m_bInitialized = true;
 
-	std::thread piplelineThread([this](){compileAllPipelines();});
-	piplelineThread.detach();
+	/* On slow / non-conformant Vulkan compilers (e.g. PanVK on Mali-G52 /
+	 * Bifrost v7), precompiling the entire shader-permutation set up front
+	 * saturates the compiler for many minutes and starves the on-demand
+	 * pipeline compile the first composite needs, so the nested present
+	 * loop appears frozen. Allow skipping the precompile; the per-frame
+	 * pipeline() path compiles (and disk-caches) what is actually needed
+	 * on demand. Unset on Adreno / RADV, behaviour is unchanged. */
+	if ( !getenv( "GAMESCOPE_DISABLE_PIPELINE_PRECOMPILE" ) )
+	{
+		std::thread piplelineThread([this](){compileAllPipelines();});
+		piplelineThread.detach();
+	}
 
 	g_reshadeManager.init(this);
 
